course: dictionary
lesson: 6852
title: Outward: away from the centre
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Outward means going away from the centre or from a place, towards the outside. Think of a ripple on a pond: it spreads outward from the place where the stone landed.
explain: «The wobble travels outwards until it reaches your ear, a bit like a push passed along a queue.» Outwards means the same as outward. The wobble starts in one place and moves away from it, so outwards is a clue for the meaning.
explain: Outward can also describe what you can see on the outside, not what is inside or felt, as in outward calm. Someone may look calm on the outside while feeling worried on the inside. An outward journey is the trip there, not the trip back.
fact: Outward means going away from the centre or from a place, towards the outside.
fact: «A salad spinner flings the water outward and off the leaves through the holes.» The water moves away from the middle of the spinner.
fact: Outward can mean what you can see on the outside, as in outward appearance.
fact: An outward journey is the trip there; the trip back is the return journey.
fact: Outwards is another form of outward and means the same thing.
exercise: «A salad spinner flings the water outward and off the leaves.» Which way does the water go? | Towards the middle of the spinner | Back into the bowl | Into the leaves | *Away from the centre, to the outside
exercise: «Her outward calm hid how nervous she felt.» What does outward mean here? | What she felt on the inside | *What can be seen on the outside | Very loud noise | A long walk to school
exercise: Ben says, «My outward journey took two hours.» Which trip took two hours? | Both trips together | A trip on the moon | The trip back home | *The trip there
test: Ripples on a pond spread outward from the stone. Where do the ripples start? | Under the bank | *At the centre, where the stone fell | Nowhere, they just appear | At the edge of the pond
test: Which phrase means the trip there, not the trip back? | short cut | *outward journey | return journey | empty journey
exam: In «outward appearance», what does outward describe? | What someone is thinking | A time of day | What is hidden inside | *What can be seen on the outside
